decisions/lang.md:## LANG-88 A generator whose output names its invoker: `Std.ownerGenerator` takes no argument and installs the one-member allowlist of the member who generated, read from the Turn's request (2026-10-26; FABLE-META-2, axis 1; DESIGN-META §8; a `lang:`, no wire change)
decisions/lang.md:## LANG-83 The document: a section is a `Std.hole` at `bytes` whose candidates are members' posts, justified by their grants, selected by an editor, withdrawn by name on revocation; its refusals name the justification that failed (2026-10-26; FABLE-CTX; design `redregg/work/promo/DESIGN-CTX.md` §2.3, §4, S0 + S1; method R-0069)
decisions/lang.md:## LANG-84 Contract pins: a hole's support may demand that the cell it cites be GOVERNED by a named law or RUN a named package, read off the cell the kernel holds; a relaw that drops the law withdraws the fill by name (2026-10-26; FABLE-CTX; DESIGN-CTX §2.5a, S2; the package wire moves to version 7; method R-0069)
decisions/lang.md:## LANG-92 A claim is a sentence the kernel refuses to let be false: `keeps inv law`, its certifying shape, and the checker proved sound (L1, 2026-10-26; FABLE-PCC; design `redregg/work/promo/DESIGN-PCC.md`; method R-0069)
decisions/lang.md:## LANG-95 `Std.head` carries the chain: `headAtTy` = `{chain, height, roots, steps}`, the head law compares it at an equal step count, `headView.at` carries it (2026-10-26; FABLE-TRUST-2, Lang/StdHead by FABLE-OWNERSHIP; DESIGN-TRUST T2 §4.2; the Protocol half and the critique are PROTOCOL-75)

