## KERNEL-32 · A turn's weights are the codec's byte counts: `Turn.logWeight` is the record's size, `Cell.weight` a cell's bytes
## KERNEL-33 · The journal is pruned to the window: bounded, every answer it gives true, and a call admitted at most once
## KERNEL-29 as built · carry state by re-genesis: `Carried`, `Receive.carry`, one tagged origin
## KERNEL-34 · The phone's read takes the leaf's bytes: KERNEL-31's last premise, discharged by CODEC's leaf decoder
