decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-38 A crash-loop window passes without a Turn: grain-launch reports its clock
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-17 ADDENDUM · Ember ratified the custody fence as built
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-40 The two-uid fence, run for real: three refutations of HOSTING-17 on its first run as `nd` and `nd-hosted`
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-41 The member socket waits for the follower's command loop, not its supervisor's bind
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-42 · The member socket: an `ok` answer is committed on the member's own World, under one premise about bytes
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-43 · The member socket, strong form: the delivered answer IS the resident's datum
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-44 · The answered row is the kept answer: the deployed Bell as a witness, joined to the strong socket
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-45 · The configured bell is the Bell: the resident checks the package it is about to serve, by its bytes
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-46 · An abandoned ring does not stall the resident's queue: measured, and stated
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-47 · The journal join is bounded by follow's own frames: `journal_committed` and `answered_row_committed` restated over an explicit path
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-48 · No refusal repeats forever: every retry the resident schedules is counted, and `retriesMax` of them in a row end it `retryExhausted` by name
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-49 · What the member says is decoded once, refused by name when it is not text, and checked to describe the configured bell
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-50 · The `stdio-leg` trust row is four trusts; the one that was a theorem away is now a theorem
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-51 · The reply reader's fuel and depth are theorems, not 12 GB teeth: `Hosting.Proofs.Reply` builds in 1.6 GB
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-52 · A real model answers the Bell: the deployed resident through keybroker, THE PIN and the Anthropic API, as an opt-in row that reads the receipt and the budget
decisions/hosting.md:## HOSTING-53 · The Bell is the agent's inbox: a ring carries an AIM and `answer` delivers the text to the aim's target as one typed nested call in the same Turn; the first target is the document's section, whose candidate is withdrawn by name when the Bell's grant is revoked

